🏦 Bank Customer Data Analysis & Insights Project
🔎 Project OverviewThis repository showcases a comprehensive data analysis project executed in Microsoft Excel utilizing a Bank Customer Dataset. 
The project demonstrates a structured workflow ranging from fundamental cell formatting to advanced data lookups, aggregation, and logical operations to extract critical customer insights.The primary objective is to analyze bank customer attributes—such as account balances, demographics, and tenure—to evaluate account health and organize data for business reporting.
🚀 Technical Skills & Implementation Breakdown
📊 i) MS Excel Foundational LevelBefore executing complex logic, I structured and prepared the raw ledger data using core Excel workflows to maintain high data integrity:Mathematical Operations: Applied basic arithmetic models (SUM, subtraction, multiplication, division, and % percentage calculation) to evaluate financial variables like interest accumulation and margin rates.Data Presentation & Layout: Structured the workbook layout using custom Borders, text alignment, and cell dimensions for professional readability.Visual Hierarchy: 
Implemented Highlighting and specific text/number Formatting (Currency, Dates, Percentages) to make the banking sheet easily scannable for corporate teams.
📈 ii) MS Excel Advanced LevelTo transform the static customer database into actionable intelligence, I implemented advanced data modeling features:a) Data Retrieval & Reference ArraysUtilized VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP, and the highly efficient XLOOKUP to seamlessly search, extract, and map customer profiles across multiple relational tables based on unique Customer IDs.b) Text Manipulation & String ManagementDeployed CONCATENATE and TEXTJOIN (with custom delimiters) to merge fragmented data strings, such as combining first/last names or building complete mailing addresses from separate columns
c) Data Aggregation & Pivot TablesConstructed dynamic Pivot Tables to segment the banking dataset. This allowed for immediate cross-sectional analysis, such as viewing total account balances by region, job classification, or credit score brackets.d) Advanced Conditional & Logical FormulasIF & IFERROR: Programmed error-handling boundaries and created new categorical groups (e.g., classifying customers as "High Net Worth" vs "Standard" based on balance thresholds).COUNTIF & SUMIF: Extracted conditional aggregates, such as counting the total number of customers in a specific city or calculating the total value of deposits for a distinct account type.DATEDIF: Calculated critical time-based metrics, such as calculating customer age or tracking customer tenure (how long they have been with the bank) based on account opening dates.
